# Repository Workflow

- Keep shared profile content public-safe. Do not copy private operating docs, private prompts, personal memory, or domain-specific private skills into shared defaults.
- Scripts remain the source of truth for install and sync behavior. Update docs and checks when script behavior changes.
- Do not modify lockfiles, generated files, build config, CI config, database migrations, or environment files unless the task explicitly requires it.
- If the tree is dirty, distinguish task changes from unrelated user changes and do not revert unrelated work.
- Use one logical change per commit when committing is requested. Commit messages use English imperative conventional format.
